This source code is published for transparency: so anyone can read exactly
what Trenchcord does — especially what does and does not leave their machine —
before trusting it with their accounts. It is source-available software, not
open-source software.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   a. Read, clone, and study the source code.
   b. Build and run Trenchcord from source to evaluate it and to verify its
      behavior (including security research and auditing).
   c. Modify the source code locally as part of that evaluation, verification,
      or research.
   d. Submit bug reports, patches, and pull requests.

2. WHAT REQUIRES A SUBSCRIPTION

   Using Trenchcord beyond evaluation — that is, running it as your actual
   Discord/Telegram dashboard, for trading, sniping, alerts, or any other
   day-to-day use — requires an active Trenchcord subscription
   (https://dashboard.trenchcord.app), regardless of whether you run an
   official build or one you compiled yourself.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   a. Redistribute this software, in source or binary form, modified or
      unmodified, inside or outside of other products.
   b. Remove, disable, or circumvent the subscription requirement, or help
      others do so.
   c. Offer Trenchcord, or software derived from it, to third parties as a
      product, service, or hosted offering.
   d. Use the "Trenchcord" name or logo, which are trademarks of the
      copyright holder and are not licensed here.

